  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Fairy Trickster feat offers a splash of extra mobility plus a powerful on-hit debuff that will make your target easy for your party to quickly defeat. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tBecause Flustering Strike is only usable PB times per long rest, you may want\n\tto wait until your Proficiency Bonus improves to take the feat so that you’ll\n\tget more value out of it. Waiting until level 8 or even 12 is totally\n\treasonable.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ability-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ability Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ability-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tThis will limit the variety of characters who can use this to classes likely\n\tto be tricksters. Rogues, Sorcerers, and Warlocks are obvious choices, but\n\tMonks and Dex-based Fighters and Paladins are also good choices.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fairy-trod-trotter",
      "heading": "Fairy Trod Trotter",
      "sourceAnchor": "fairy-trod-trotter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fairy-trod-trotter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tNeat, but probably only useful for Monks and Rogues. The benefit is\n\tsituational by design, and you’ll likely go long periods without it being\n\tuseful unless your party likes to create difficult terrain.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-flustering-strike",
      "heading": "Flustering Strike",
      "sourceAnchor": "flustering-strike",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-flustering-strike-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tOnly PB times per day, but still incredibly powerful. Use this on\n\thigh-priority targets, then have your allies drop a whole bunch of hurt if\n\tyour target fails their save. Follow this with your party’s favorite\n\tsave-or-suck effects, such as Topple weapons, Stunning Strike, spells like\n\tHold Monster, etc.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
